+- Code/Performance optimizations (no gameplay change)
+
+Also added `findInfoTypeNumOrFail(...)` for older `CvUtil.findInfoTypeNum(...)` callsites that need getter/count function. Note: now also double-checked by a GitHub workflow check which now blocks new raw static/literal Python info-type lookups unless they are explicitly listed as dynamic/guarded legacy exceptions.
+C++ signature cleanup: collapsed safe multiline C++ function declarations/definitions to one physical line across the DLL source, making signatures easier to grep, compare, and review in diffs/LLM-assisted passes. Done with the help of the new `collapse_cpp_signatures.py` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/LLM_Helpers/README.md#collapse_cpp_signaturespy), a conservative signature-only helper, which intentionally skips ordinary multiline calls and unsafe comments, while also supporting traceable hoisting for reviewed whole-line comments inside signatures; review its output as a mechanical source-cleanup tool rather than a general C++ formatter. It was empirically idempotent after the first full DLL pass (rerunning reported no safe C++ signature collapses found). This is especially useful for overloaded functions like `void addMessage`, or e.g., `void CvDeal::endTrade(TradeData trade, PlayerTypes eFromPlayer, PlayerTypes eToPlayer, bool bTeam, /* advc.036: */ bool bUpdateAttitude, PlayerTypes eCancelPlayer) // advc.130p`, instead of its old three-line equivalent. See notably: https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/27
+C++ inline-return cleanup: collapsed simple inline DLL header functions whose bodies were exactly one `return` statement to one physical line, making trivial getters/wrappers easier to grep and compare. Done with the help of `collapse_cpp_inline_returns.py` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/LLM_Helpers/README.md#collapse_cpp_inline_returnspy), a conservative mechanical helper that skips constructors/destructors, multi-statement bodies, body comments, multiline signatures, and overlong results. For example, `int getGoldPerTurnByPlayer(PlayerTypes ePlayer) const { return m_aiGoldPerTurnByPlayer.get(ePlayer); } // Exposed to Python`, instead of its old four-line equivalent.
+Build cleanup - disabled unneeded DLL test code in normal builds: compile-gated disabled reproducibility-test code (`ReproTest.cpp`) so normal DLL builds no longer compile it unless explicitly enabled for debugging. This keeps dormant test/debug code out of normal builds, may slightly reduce DLL/build size, and does not change gameplay. Found with the help of the new `find_cpp_dead_code_candidates.py` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/LLM_Helpers/find_cpp_dead_code_candidates.py) LLM/manual-review helper.
+GitHub workflow build checks: added GitHub Actions checks under `.github/workflows` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/tree/main/.github/workflows/) to catch forgotten debug/default settings and data drift at each commit. Current checks notably verify launch-guard sentinel values, XML tag references in SAS define text values, integer SAS define bounds, valid main-menu opening-music script setup, disabled BBAI logging defaults, shared UI font defaults, Sevopedia Leader AI Personality Panel predumped-cache defaults and predump file presence, `WorldSizeTypes` enum/XML alignment, `CvGameCoreDLL/Project/temp_files/` staying effectively empty (only its tracked placeholder file), not being ignored by `.gitignore`, and being allowed only as an archive-excluded development marker through `.gitattributes` (helps catch stale fast-compile temp files. We check this because we suspect fast compiles can be unreliable, and also helps catch forgetting to replace the committed DLL after compiling; see KI#38 and KI#38.2), and every playable `PrivateMaps/*.py` being listed exactly once across the SAS map-script heaviness/coverage defines while every listed map script exists in `PrivateMaps/`. For example, this helped spot map scripts that were previously unclassified in SAS map-script heaviness defines (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27198308080/job/80295526028); they are now listed explicitly for exhaustiveness (more robust; no gameplay change). See notably: https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/29
+AIP predump refresh bot: added `aip-predump-refresh.yml` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/.github/workflows/aip-predump-refresh.yml), a tested GitHub Actions bot workflow for the Sevopedia Leader AI Personality predump cache. The existing checker still fails when the committed predump is stale, but the refresh workflow can now run `aip_predump_values.py --write` outside Civ4 and open/update a bot PR containing only `SevoPediaLeaderCachePredumped.py` when real generated AIP data or display-label drift is detected. It runs automatically after pushes to known AIP predump dependency files. Tested in PR #31 (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/31) with no-op, XML comment-only, numeric Leader XML, and Python label/display drift cases, so harmless comments do not refresh the cache while real generated predump changes do. See notably: https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/31
+Other examples: This notably also helped spot and fix duplicate text, parent, and child XML keys found by new GitHub workflow check text (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27332010214/job/80746523894), parent (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27258698041/job/80498936912), and child (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27336768909/job/80762873956) (See KI#148, KI#149, KI#150), and suspicious malformed-looking XML tag punctuation (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27342682844/job/80783239087) (e.g., `<French>>`, `</English>>`) (see KI#151) and XML suspicious text chars (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27400470104/job/80977135402) (see KI#152). The checks also run locally with Python 3; see `.github/workflows/README.md` current build checks (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/.github/workflows/README.md#current-build-checks).
+Python Ruff GitHub workflow: added `python-ruff.yml` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/.github/workflows/python-ruff.yml), which prints a full Ruff report and fails on a practical critical gate for syntax/parse errors and Pyflakes bug checks. This helped spot shadowed duplicate callbacks in base Civ4 `Oasis.py` (see KI#164) and a Base AdvCiv bug of dormant undefined `Point` (instead of using `PointLayout`) helper in `RectLayout.py` (see KI#165).
+Python 2.4 Docker compile GitHub workflow: added `python24-compile.yml` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/.github/workflows/python24-compile.yml), which runs `Assets/Python` and `PrivateMaps` through real CPython 2.4 syntax/bytecode compilation using our separate `wonderingabout/python-2.4-docker` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/python-2.4-docker) GHCR image. This complements Ruff by checking the old parser Civ4 embeds, without launching Civ4 or importing engine-only modules. A deliberate test confirmed it fails (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27897204427) on Python 2.5+ ternary syntax such as `SAS_MAGIC_PY24_COMPILE_BREAK_TEST = 1 if True else 0` in `SASMagicNumbers.py`. See `.github/workflows/README.md` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/.github/workflows/README.md#python-24-compile-workflow), and README.md (Python Scripts) (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/README.md#python-scripts) for screenshots.
+Light source archive helper: added `make_light_source_zip.py` (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/LLM_Helpers/README.md#make_light_source_zippy), which creates a timestamped no-compression AdvCiv-SAS source/data/docs archive under `LLM_Helpers/outputs` or a chosen output folder. This avoids repeatedly manually selecting and tediously creating an updated ZIP of each file/folder each time, of the same useful core files/folders ChatGPT or other LLMs can read or needs, while leaving unneeded or too heavy to use ones (e.g., as of now no .fpk, .tga, .dll, or pycache folders, art assets folder), when sharing compact mod context with local tools or LLMs.
+Dependabot for GitHub Actions: added Dependabot tracking for GitHub Actions versions to help address Node.js runtime deprecation warnings such as `actions/<hidden-email>` and `actions/<hidden-email>` still using Node.js 20 (see <hidden-email>#24 (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/24)). This should reduce manual maintenance and make future action-version updates easier to notice and apply. See `.github/workflows/README.md` current build checks (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/.github/workflows/README.md#current-build-checks).
+land/water bonus-specific builds/improvements caching (`CvPlot::SAS_getBonusSpecificBuild`):
+Load Precomputed Files: For modders, CI now checks that the committed predump still matches leader XML/shared AIP display logic; if it fails, `aip_predump_values.py --write` can refresh the file outside Civ4. This checker notably caught 394 stale label entries, such as `Build Unit (52)` missing the updated `Build Unit % (52)` text and then helped generate an updated predump. The old manual in-game `PythonDbg.log` dump path remains a manual fallback or alternative way of refreshing the predump.
+Timestamped BBAI log files: Optionally log each new game and loaded save to a new UTC-timestamped file (e.g., `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_new1.log` or `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_load2.log`) instead of expanding the existing `BBAI.log`, which was very tedious to clean up or identify/store/read/review/upload, and so repeated save-file tests no longer require restarting Civ4. Each log begins notably with the new/load time, currently active BBAI log levels, turn/year, map and game settings (including `landheavy` and `navalheavy` actual game information), player counts, and RNG states, avoiding mixed logs and the need to restart Civ4 between repeated save-file tests. See also README.md (BBAI logging head example) (https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/blob/main/README.md#bbai-logging-head-example).
+BBAI worker log split: added separate worker and Work Boat / `UNITAI_WORKER_SEA` BBAI log-level defines so ordinary `SAS_BBAI_UNIT_LOG_LEVEL` can focus on non-worker unit behavior such as scrapping, army movement, and combat-unit decisions. Worker and worker-sea logs had become noisy enough to hide those unit decisions, and Work Boats use distinct logic from land workers, so they now have their own category as well.
+BBAI Settler log split: added `SAS_BBAI_SETTLER_LOG_LEVEL`, separated from UNIT so Settlers and other units can be inspected independently. This notably covers city-site decisions and Settler movement, scouting, returns, and founding; FOUND as of now separately controls detailed city-site scoring calculations. This notably lets UNIT investigate other unit behavior without enabling the multi-megabyte first-city Settler traces needed for example for the Berlin, Karakorum, and Cuzco regression tests.
+Culture-victory BBAI diagnostics: added a new dedicated `SAS_BBAI_CULTURE_LOG_LEVEL` notably for diagnosing premature, uneven, or wasteful AI culture investment without enabling broad player/city logs. It records for example culture-stage reasons, current/projected Legendary-city countdowns and rival ranking, competing victory progress, actual culture-slider decisions, per-city weights and production, and culture contributed by production processes and assigned specialists.
+Citizen-allocation BBAI diagnostics: added a dedicated `SAS_BBAI_CITIZEN_LOG_LEVEL` notably for finding worked plots or specialists that the AI's full city-aware comparison would replace, but its faster preliminary selection overlooked. At the highest level, it also reports suspicious worked/unworked plot pairs under a simple food-first yield check.
+Evacuation and retreat BBAI diagnostics: added `SAS_BBAI_EVACUATION_LOG_LEVEL`. It notably helps investigate evacuation/retreat behavior without broad city or unit logging, for doomed cities, workers, and naval units.
+Minor remove unused SAS Huge player fallback
+Remove SAS world-size magic numbers: Add AdvCiv-SAS world sizes to the DLL/Python WorldSizeTypes enum so C++ and Python now match CIV4WorldInfo.xml order directly, including Arena and SAS24/SAS32/SAS40/SAS48
+Replace the old SAS_MAGIC_WORLDSIZE_* workaround in map scripts and helper code with WorldSizeTypes.WORLDSIZE_* constants. Update the world-size workflow check to verify XML/DLL/Python enum alignment and catch old runtime magic-number references.
+Also document and disable vanilla BtS-compatible replay storage for AdvCiv-SAS replays. SAS intentionally shifts raw XML ids for game speeds, world sizes, and handicaps, so replays should use the normal mod replay format instead of pretending to be vanilla BtS-compatible. See KI#166.
+Add C++ dead-code candidate helper and gate disabled ReproTest code: Add an LLM/manual-review helper that scans the DLL source for conservative dead-code candidates. Use the first report result to compile-gate ReproTest.cpp behind ENABLE_REPRO_TEST, keeping dormant reproducibility-test code out of normal builds while preserving the feature when explicitly enabled. This is a build/binary cleanup and does not change gameplay.
